    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Brahmo Samaj spearheaded early intellectual reform, advocating monotheism and the abolition of social evils like Sati.",
        "Arya Samaj advocated a revivalist approach based on Vedic authority, promoting social service and educational institutions.",
        "Aligarh Movement sought to modernize Muslim society through Western education and scientific rationalism.",
        "Ramakrishna Mission synthesized Indian spirituality with selfless service to humanity (Practical Vedanta).",
        "Legislative reforms targeting women's rights, such as widow remarriage and child marriage restriction, formed the bedrock of social progress."
      ],
      "id": "r4wwas5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8md16p7",
      "content": "The 19th century socio-religious reform movements emerged as a response to social stagnation, religious orthodoxy, caste rigidity, gender inequality, colonial critique, and the impact of Western liberal thought. These movements attempted reinterpretation of religious texts, elimination of social evils, modernization of education, and creation of a rational public sphere."
    },
    {
      "id": "1offpsp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. COMMON FEATURES OF REFORM MOVEMENTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "atwtfw4",
      "content": "• Use of rationalism and reinterpretation of scriptures."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "na5tcbi",
      "content": "• Critique of idol worship and ritualism (in many movements)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g5a6sqr",
      "content": "• Emphasis on women education and widow remarriage."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b4i0ji9",
      "content": "• Attack on caste discrimination (varying intensity)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5eelzn9",
      "content": "• Establishment of schools, journals, associations."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ojd3skr",
      "content": "• Creation of middle-class leadership and proto-national consciousness."
    },
    {
